    "title": "Man dies following water incident - NewsBreak",
    "text": "DUCK KEY — An 82-year-old Stuart man died Wednesday, July 30, after being found unresponsive in Florida Bay waters approximately 5 miles off mile marker 60. Clarence Shawver was snorkeling when he was found at 10:45 a.m., taken ashore and transported to Fishermen’s Community Hospital in Marathon, where he was pronounced dead, according to the Monroe County Sheriff's Office. Foul play is not believed to be a factor in the incident. Autopsy results are pending.",
